.SH "NAME"
nvme-show-regs \- Reads and shows the defined NVMe controller registers for NVMe over PCIe or the controller properties for NVMe over Fabrics\&.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIshow\-regs\fR <device>
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Reads and shows the controller registers\&. For an NVMe over PCIe controller, nvme maps its PCI memory space through sysfs (the resource0 file of the PCI device) and reads them there\&. For an NVMe over Fabrics controller, it reads its properties with Property Get commands: CAP, VS, CC, CSTS and the ones of NSSR, NSSD and CRTO the controller implements\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and must be the nvme admin character device (ex: /dev/nvme0)\&.
.sp
With \-v, the fields of each register are shown decoded\&. The JSON output has the value of each register under its name, with \-v an object of the value and its decoded fields\&. The binary output is the registers from 0h to E1Bh, as they are in the PCI memory space, with zeros for the ones not read\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&. Other versions are rejected\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-quiet
.RS 4
Suppress informational messages\&. Errors are still reported, and \-\-quiet cancels any \-\-verbose for the library log level\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-set\-options=<key=value>[,<key=value>\&...]
.RS 4
Set libnvme library options for this invocation\&. Supported keys are
\fIforce\-4k\fR,
\fImi\-probe\-enabled\fR,
\fItest\-base\-dir\fR
and
\fItest\-sysfs\-dir\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
\fIinfinite\fR
or
\fI\-1\fR
waits without a time limit (0xffffffff)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Show the NVMe over PCIe controller registers or the NVMe over Fabric controller properties in a binary format:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
# nvme show\-regs /dev/nvme0 \-o binary
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Show the NVMe over PCIe controller registers or the NVMe over Fabric controller properties in a human readable format:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
# nvme show\-regs /dev/nvme0 \-v
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Show the NVMe over PCIe controller registers or NVMe\-oF controller properties in a json format:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
# nvme show\-regs /dev/nvme0 \-o json
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.RE
